From 6ce075d00272c2a0a89836efd08359afe4365673 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hang(Harry) Gao <GaohRyan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 02:35:34 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] opt: sim-to-real randomisation (action delay; armature,
 kp, kd, joint damping, friction loss)

Not in the paper or the official release. Two switches, both off by default:
- env.action_delay_max N: each env executes the action computed d ~ U{0..N} control steps ago (per
  episode). The replay stores the executed action, so the world model needs no change; imagination
  feeds it the action from d steps back while reward and observations keep the clean action.
- env.sim2real_dr: per-env armature scale (startup), kp / kd scale, passive damping and friction loss
  (reset). The five scalars are appended to the world-model context xi (33 -> 38): the actor only
  becomes robust to what the world model can vary in imagination.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
